    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0288" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1742</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-05T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 5, 1917, 5 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of January 15, 6 p.m. Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs on
                    February 3 stated to Guthrie that he had not heard of any protests made to China
                    against negotiations for American loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
